WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.004
Tributes are pouring in for Matthew Perry,
the actor best known for his role

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.382
as Chandler
Bing in the smash hit sitcom Friends.

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:08.216
Fans in New York

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:12.137
set up a makeshift memorial outside
the apartment made famous by the show

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:16.266
Saturday Night Live honored
Perry, who hosted that program

00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:19.352
26 years ago during the height of Friends

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:23.815
singer Adele even passed her
show in Las Vegas to share a few words.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:24.399
Listen

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:29.821
So my favorite memories
of when I was younger with my friends

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.489
and one of my friends answered

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:34.868
when I was like 12,
get the best Chandler impression.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.454
And he with her
all the time to make us laugh.

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:39.622
And if any of us are having a bad day
or feeling those,

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:41.666
you just pretend to be Chandler.

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:45.962
And I remember that character
for the rest of my life and all of it.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:50.675
You know, for the first time,
I heard your friends call

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:55.430
me because
I was so them with his struggles

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.142
with addiction and sobriety, which I think
is incredibly, incredibly brave.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:02.562
And yeah, just how much I love

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:05.023
what he did to feel special
to what he did to me.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.777
Now, the co-creators of Friends
are remembering

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:12.781
Perry, saying in a joint statement,
We are shocked and deeply, deeply saddened

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:16.826
by our beloved friend Matthew's passing
it still seems impossible.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:21.956
All we can say is that we feel blessed
to have had him as part of our lives.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.418
Perry was found dead in his Los Angeles
home on Saturday.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:29.089
That's according to the Los Angeles Times,
which cited law enforcement sources.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.048
Authorities say

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:31.925
there were no signs of foul play

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.636
in an investigation
into the cause of death is underway.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.680
Matthew Perry was 54 years old.

00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:39.557
Rebecca Sun is a senior editor

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:42.227
at The Hollywood Reporter,
and she joins me now from Las Vegas.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:45.313
What a nice tribute from Adele
and she really voiced

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:48.942
what so many people,
strangers really loved about both

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.654
his character on friends
and the man himself.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:56.407
What have you learned about the reaction
in the last 24 hours?

00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:57.367
It's just been stunning.

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:01.496
I think that the reaction was,

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:04.249
as Matthew Perry said last year,
actually during his

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.794
book tour, that people might be shocked

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:12.298
but not surprised by news of his death,
which is really quite sad.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.718
I think that he was so public
and open about his struggles

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:19.430
with addiction
that as soon as the news broke you know,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:23.643
I think anybody who was somewhat familiar
with him, even his fans,

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:27.856
you kind of had a sinking feeling about
perhaps what might have been the cause

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.276
But, you know, he was so beloved.

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:35.405
I think that Chandler's certainly for me
as well as fans around

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:38.616
the world is truly like Adele said,
one of the great characters

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:39.909
in television history.

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:40.660
Absolutely.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.580
And so many generations
can relate to that.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.831
And so many people

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.917
all over the world, Friends was dubbed
into so many different languages.

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:49.586
I want to show you now,

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:52.589
you know, we've had a lot of reaction,
but one of them also from Canadian

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:57.343
Prime Minister Justin Trudeau,
who tweeted or I should say is said on X.

00:02:57.552 --> 00:03:00.305
Matthew Perry's
passing is shocking and saddening.

00:03:00.555 --> 00:03:03.308
We'll never forget the schoolyard games
we used to play.

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:04.350
And I know people around

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.687
the world are never going to forget
the joy he brought them.

00:03:07.729 --> 00:03:10.064
Thanks for all the laughs, Matthew.

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:14.319
I mean, this is the kind of outpouring
that we've had

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:16.029
and many people may not have known here.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:20.408
He had a fairly really normal
upbringing in Canada

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:22.869
before he returned to the United States
for his acting career.

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:26.623
Well, some people are wondering about,
though, I have to ask you, is

00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:29.792
we haven't heard from the fellow
cast members yet.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:30.335
Why not?

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:33.671
I think that

00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:38.468
I imagine that as the people
who were among the closest to him,

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:42.263
certainly professionally,
they probably need to take some time,

00:03:42.263 --> 00:03:45.850
you know, for themselves
to to process this.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:51.064
You know, I know that their reaction
is what those of us

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:54.025
who kind of only know them
as the group of friends, you know,

00:03:54.108 --> 00:03:55.777
they're
the ones we're waiting for the most,

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:58.905
but they need to emotionally process
this themselves.

00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:02.283
They they had an intense, unique
one of a kind experience

00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:05.078
that only the six of them
shared for an entire decade.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.373
They might, you know, want to be talking

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:11.918
to one another and seeing if they want
to make some sort of group statement.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.170
But but but I think that's what it is.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:18.758
I think that it speaks to the magnitude
of this type of loss to them that,

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:21.928
you know,
they're not doing some sort of quick,

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:24.639
quick reaction on Instagram, not just yet.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:25.723
Yeah.

00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:29.060
As you said, the magnitude of the loss
that everyone is still dealing with.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.939
If we deal with his acting career, though,
I mean, it has been said that,

00:04:33.815 --> 00:04:36.192
you know, as shocking, perhaps the details

00:04:36.192 --> 00:04:39.195
of his personal life was his performance

00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:44.033
was comforting in his consistency
and its comedic timing on friends.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.037
You always waited for that line
from Chandler Bing to see what

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:48.788
he would come up with.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:50.748
Exactly.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:54.460
I mean, I think that the show creators,
you know, have said before

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.089
that initially he was
his character was the hardest to cast.

00:04:58.506 --> 00:05:01.259
They thought it was Chandler
just really badly written,

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:03.177
you know,
why is this guy so hard to cast in?

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:07.140
As soon as Matthew Perry walked in
for his audition and Matthew said

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.894
that he had sort of he was the one
who created that unique Chandler cadence.

00:05:11.894 --> 00:05:14.063
Could I be any more funny?

00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:17.525
You know, that I everybody around
the world knows that.

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:19.902
And that was what he brought
to the character.

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:23.323
And as a result, that that combination

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:26.367
of screenwriting dialog and performance

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:29.245
you know, created
the magic of Chandler and.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.749
And yeah, it's it's

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:35.585
that's a legacy that will always live on.

00:05:35.585 --> 00:05:35.960
Yeah.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.670
And in terms of what we have to say, it

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.006
it is sad
he wrote it himself in his memoir.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:43.176
But do you believe it in
so doing though, that definitely

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:46.929
he kind of gave resolution to everything
that happened throughout his career.

00:05:46.929 --> 00:05:47.138
Right.

00:05:47.138 --> 00:05:51.059
Because he got to write about it himself
in that memoir that that came out about a

00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:51.476
year ago.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.144
Yeah.

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:56.981
I mean, I think that and it's eerie
because it was almost exactly a year ago

00:05:56.981 --> 00:06:00.485
that the memoir came out in the memoir,
you know, I think maybe people were

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:05.615
sort of expecting a typical celebrity
memoir out, most of it being showbiz

00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:06.157
stories.

00:06:06.157 --> 00:06:10.912
But really a lot of it, it's
about his lifelong battle with addiction.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:16.417
And and he says somewhere and it's a quote
that's going viral on social media today

00:06:16.417 --> 00:06:20.630
that he knows that his legacy people are
it's going to be friends, is going to be,

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.592
you know, the first, second
and third paragraph of his obituary.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:29.347
But what he hoped his legacy would be
would be to give hope to anybody who's

00:06:29.347 --> 00:06:34.394
struggling with addiction and substance
abuse through sort of opening up his life.

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:39.273
And so I am glad that he had the ability
to really complete that book

00:06:39.524 --> 00:06:42.276
and to get out there and tell that story,
because I think that's

00:06:42.276 --> 00:06:43.486
what he wants to be.

00:06:43.486 --> 00:06:45.822
He wanted to be remembered it was so for.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.825
It was certainly an act of courage
from someone who remember

00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:50.159
really for their comedy.

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:53.496
And as you said,
it will be an indelible moment

00:06:53.496 --> 00:06:56.791
for all of us when we remember
how he reached out to people and said,

00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:57.875
I want to help people.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:06:59.460
I want them to know they are not alone.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.088
Rebecca, Sam, we have to leave it there.
Thanks so much. Appreciate it.

